      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum:\n- Immediate-release metformin: 2550 mg/day maximum (usually given as 850 mg three times daily)\n- Extended-release metformin: 2000 mg/day maximum\n\nAbove these limits, the risk of GI side effects and lactic acidosis goes up without much added effect on blood sugar.\n\n**You may have meant one of these:**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, split as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n3. Something else, such as 1000 mg twice daily\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give a brief reason, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose above the labeled maximum."
      }
     ],
